      "note": "Flags :role and :status as mass-assignable on the Owner-only staff endpoint. The Owner guard alone is NOT the reason this is safe: the threat is an unattended Owner session, which already satisfies require_owner!. What closes it is that no request can mint an Owner. Workforce::CreateStaff::ASSIGNABLE_ROLES is %w[staff manager], and anything else raises Invalid before a User is built; Workforce::UpdateStaff writes neither role nor any User field except :email, so there is no path that promotes an existing account. Covered by spec/requests/api/v1/workforce_admin_spec.rb, 'refuses to mint an Owner, even for the Owner'. Delete this entry rather than re-fingerprinting it if ASSIGNABLE_ROLES ever gains 'owner', or if UpdateStaff starts writing role."
